<title>SRI LANKA: Three Acre up sharply on expansion news.</title>
<headline>Three Acre up sharply on expansion news.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Acre Farms Ltd rose 27 percent or six rupees to 28, on a small volume of 200 shares as retailers hunted the scrip after the company announced expansion plans, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The share is not liquid which pushes up the price even on slight demand,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>The company, which supplies day-old chicks, said it was expanding by buying a local firm which owns a piggery, hatchery and retail outlets, at a cost of 280 million rupees. --Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
